  "text_sanskrit": "शुभाशुभफलैरेवं मोक्ष्यसे कर्मबन्धनैः । संन्यासयोगयुक्तात्मा विमुक्तो मामुपैष्यसि ॥ ९-२८ ॥",
  "itrans": "shubhAshubhaphalairevaM mokShyase karmabandhanaiH . sa.nnyAsayogayuktAtmA vimukto mAmupaiShyasi .. 9-28 ..",
  "translation": "Thus, thou shalt be freed from the bonds of Karma yielding good and evil fruits; having united in thyself the Sanyasa and Yoga, thou shalt, being released, come unto Me. (29)  V. Sanyasa is to renounce the fruit of duties and virtuous deeds performed. Yoga is the performance of such duties and virtuous deeds enjoined upon man. (28) A. As stated above, “I accept what is offered with devotion.” if Thou art beloved of the devout, it follows Thou art displeased with the haters. Then, bearing love and hatred to the devout and tire hater, Thou art likely to bestow great blessings on the somewhat devout and to inflict very severe punishments (great evil) upon one whose hatred is not very intense. So do I find Kings and Lords of men behaving. Thus, partiality and cruelty seems to find place in Thee. To correct this absurd view Sri Krishna says:",
